# STEP 11 — lead storage. Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# .env.local is git-ignored. Never commit real values, and never give any of
# these the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix — that prefix is what tells Next.js to inline
# a value into the JavaScript the browser downloads. Everything below is
# read only inside /api/leads, which runs on the server.

# ---- Where leads go: a Google Sheet
# 1. Create a Google Sheet.
# 2. Extensions -> Apps Script, paste the doPost() script from the project
#    README, and Deploy -> New deployment -> Web app
#    (Execute as: Me, Who has access: Anyone).
# 3. Paste the deployment URL here. Every submitted enquiry becomes one row.
LEADS_SHEET_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ---- Abuse protection
# Any long random string. Peppers the SHA-256 of the requester's IP so the
# rate-limit counters can't be reversed back to addresses.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
RATE_LIMIT_SALT=

# ---- Origin check
# The site's own public URL, e.g. https://ab-rehman-portfolio.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=
